# Build context exclusions.
#
# This file did not exist until Phase 7, and its absence was not cosmetic. `COPY . .` in the
# builder stage runs one line AFTER the Linux `node_modules` is copied from `deps`, so without
# these rules the HOST's node_modules — Windows-resolved, carrying `.CMD`/`.ps1` shims and win32
# native binaries for sharp and @node-rs/argon2 — overwrote it. The image then failed at runtime
# in a way that looks nothing like its cause.
#
# The second thing it stopped: `.env` (real secrets) entering the image. `next build` auto-loads
# `.env`, so an unignored one is both baked into a layer and silently authoritative over the
# container environment the compose sets. Invariant 7 says no secrets in code; a secret in an
# image layer is worse, because it ships.

# --- dependencies: always reinstalled inside the image for the target platform ---
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- secrets: never. .env.example is not needed in the image either ---
.env
.env.*

# --- build output: regenerated by the builder stage ---
.next
out
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- version control and CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- test and local runtime artefacts ---
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright
.tmp
.pgdata
.pgdata-e2e
storage

# --- editor / OS ---
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- documentation and deployment descriptors ---
# The image never reads these, and excluding them keeps the context small enough that a rebuild
# over a slow link is not an event. Note `docker/` IS excluded: its init SQL is bind-mounted by
# the compose file into the postgres container, never copied into the app image.
#
# `*.md` matches one path segment, so this covers CLAUDE.md and TODO.md at the root and leaves
# prisma/GLOBAL_TABLES.md alone — which is correct: it travels with the schema it documents.
docs
docker
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
Caddyfile
*.md
